      "evidence": "template/scripts/lifecycle_workers.py (diff ~L1632-1657): `gate_scratch = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix=\"lifecycle-preflight-\")` is created before `work_next(...)`. `gate_scratch.cleanup()` runs after the `if args.run ... raise WorkerError(\"no job claimed; refused ...\")` block, with no try/finally. Wrapping the use in `with`/`try-finally` would make this deterministic.",
      "id": "gate-scratch-dir-leak-on-error",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The provider-gate scratch directory is only cleaned on the straight-line path. If work_next raises, for example a WorkerError, an EnvironmentFailure or the 'no job claimed; refused' error, the cleanup is skipped. The TemporaryDirectory is then removed only when it is garbage collected."
